{{template "head" .}}
  <section class="sud-hero">
    <div class="sud-hero-bg"></div>
    <div class="sud-hero-grid"></div>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="spacer">
        <p class="sud-eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span>THE NSM EXPERIENCE &nbsp;·&nbsp; MADE FOR YOUR CITY</p>
        <h1 class="sud-h1">Your city.<br><span class="grad">Your way.</span></h1>
        <p class="sud-lead">A more personal Grand Theft Auto V multiplayer. Custom dedicated servers, shareable join links and fair Keymaster slots, powered by <strong>AFX</strong> — all in one place.</p>
        <div class="players sud-live"><span class="live-dot"></span>Join the <strong><span class="current-players" data-stat="players">{{kfmt (index .Stats "Players")}}</span></strong>&nbsp;people playing right now</div>
        <div class="sud-btn-row">
          <div class="btnpadder" style="position:relative">
            <a id="dl" href="/download" data-no-spa="1">
              <span class="txt">DOWNLOAD CLIENT</span>
              <span class="desc">NSM.exe &nbsp;·&nbsp; Windows 10 &amp; 11</span>
            </a>
          </div>
          <a class="sud-ghost" href="/servers">Browse the server list <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </div>
        <p class="plaText">By downloading, you agree to the <a href="/docs">NSM Terms of Service</a></p>
        <p class="sud-meta">Windows 10 &amp; 11 &nbsp;·&nbsp; 64-bit &nbsp;·&nbsp; 8 GB RAM minimum &nbsp;·&nbsp; Free to play</p>
        <div class="sud-quick">
          <a href="/servers">Server List</a>
          <a href="/keymaster">Keymaster</a>
          <a href="/forum">Forum</a>
          <a href="/docs">Docs</a>
          <a href="/support">Support</a>
          <a href="/status">Status</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
<main>

<section class="sud-section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="spacer">
      <p class="sud-eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span>THE NSM PLATFORM</p>
      <h2 class="sud-h2">A familiar place.<br><span class="grad">A different feeling.</span></h2>
      <p class="sud-lead">Everything you need to find a server, join your friends and run your own city — designed around the way you actually play.</p>
      <div class="sud-grid cols-3">
        <article class="sud-card">
          <span class="sud-tag">Live list</span>
          <h3>Find your people.</h3>
          <p>Browse and filter community servers live on the web or inside NSM.exe, with real player counts and instant one-click connection.</p>
          <a class="sud-card-link" href="/servers">Open the server list <span class="arrow">→</span></a>
        </article>
        <article class="sud-card">
          <span class="sud-tag">Join links</span>
          <h3>Share without the IP.</h3>
          <p>Every listed server gets a short, shareable <code>/join/</code> link that hides the raw address. Connections stay clean and private.</p>
          <a class="sud-card-link" href="/docs">How join links work <span class="arrow">→</span></a>
        </article>
        <article class="sud-card">
          <span class="sud-tag">AFX Portal</span>
          <h3>Your server, your keys.</h3>
          <p>Issue license keys, watch live heartbeats and manage upvotes from the Keymaster. 2,048 slots are free without a key.</p>
          <a class="sud-card-link" href="/keymaster">Open AFX Portal <span class="arrow">→</span></a>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sud-section tight">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="spacer">
      <p class="sud-sublabel">the numbers</p>
      <div class="sud-grid cols-4">
        <article class="sud-card">
          <span class="num" data-stat="players">{{kfmt (index .Stats "Players")}}</span>
          <h3>playing right now</h3>
          <p>Live across every listed NSM server, updating as people join and leave.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="sud-card">
          <span class="num" data-stat="servers">{{index .Stats "Servers"}}</span>
          <h3>live servers</h3>
          <p>Whitelisted roleplay, freeroam and everything in between.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="sud-card">
          <span class="num">2,048</span>
          <h3>slots per server</h3>
          <p>Full OneSync entity and population sync, free with no key required.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="sud-card">
          <span class="num">10</span>
          <h3>free upvotes</h3>
          <p>Every account gets ten free upvotes to boost the servers you love.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sud-section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="spacer">
      <p class="sud-eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span>BUILT ON AFX &nbsp;·&nbsp; POWERED BY THE COMMUNITY</p>
      <h2 class="sud-h2">Built around <span class="grad">the way you play.</span></h2>
      <p class="sud-lead">Years of development on the <strong>AFX</strong> framework, which has played a giant role in the modding community — NSM offers a huge range of features:</p>
      <div class="sud-grid cols-4">
        <article class="sud-card">
          <span class="material-icons-outlined">cloud_download</span>
          <h3>Streaming</h3>
          <p>NSM allows servers to use custom cars, maps, weapons, and more dynamically.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="sud-card">
          <span class="material-icons-outlined">sync_alt</span>
          <h3>Sync quality</h3>
          <p>NSM uses the original network code, improved upon by AFX OneSync, so you'll have the best sync around.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="sud-card">
          <span class="material-icons-outlined">groups</span>
          <h3>OneSync</h3>
          <p>Play with up to 2048 players on a single dedicated server with full entity and population synchronization.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="sud-card">
          <span class="material-icons-outlined">shield</span>
          <h3>Standalone</h3>
          <p>NSM does not interact with the Rockstar Online Services other than to validate your game copy when you first launch it.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="sud-card">
          <span class="material-icons-outlined">dns</span>
          <h3>Dedicated servers</h3>
          <p>Browse and filter community servers live in NSM.exe or on the web, with instant one-click connection.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="sud-card">
          <span class="material-icons-outlined">vpn_key</span>
          <h3>AFX Portal</h3>
          <p>Issue and manage server license keys, view active heartbeats, and link your AFX account directly in NSM.exe.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="sud-card">
          <span class="material-icons-outlined">code</span>
          <h3>Lua, C# &amp; JS</h3>
          <p>Build rich gamemodes, NUI interfaces, and custom gameplay systems using Lua, C#, or JavaScript runtimes.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="sud-card">
          <span class="material-icons-outlined">forum</span>
          <h3>Community</h3>
          <p>Share releases, discuss scripts, and discover resources on the AFX Forum and AFX Marketplace.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sud-section tight">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="spacer">
      <p class="sud-eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span>NOW AVAILABLE</p>
      <div class="sud-card" style="padding:2.25rem 2.1rem">
        <span class="ea-badge">Now Available</span>
        <h2 class="sud-h2" style="margin-top:1rem">Now supporting Grand Theft Auto V Enhanced</h2>
        <p class="sud-lead" style="margin-bottom:1.35rem">Jump into customized dedicated servers with the NSM desktop client, browse the live server list, and manage your server keys in AFX Portal.</p>
        <div class="sud-btn-row" style="margin-bottom:0">
          <a class="sud-ghost" href="/servers">Open Live Server List <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
          <span class="dl-text"><strong data-stat="servers">{{index .Stats "Servers"}}</strong> live servers &middot; <strong data-stat="players">{{kfmt (index .Stats "Players")}}</strong> players online</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sud-section" id="requirements">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="spacer">
      <p class="sud-sublabel">system requirements</p>
      <h2 class="sud-h2">Know before <span class="grad">you go.</span></h2>
      <div class="sud-grid cols-2">
        <article class="sud-card sud-specs">
          <h3>Recommended</h3>
          <table class="stat-table">
            <tr><td class="stat">CPU</td><td>Intel Core i5 3470 @ 3.2GHz / AMD X8 FX-8350 @ 4GHz</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="stat">GPU</td><td>NVIDIA GTX 660 2GB / AMD HD 7870 2GB</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="stat">RAM</td><td>16GB</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="stat">HDD</td><td>72GB + ~8GB for NSM cache</td></tr>
          </table>
        </article>
        <article class="sud-card sud-specs">
          <h3>Minimum</h3>
          <table class="stat-table">
            <tr><td class="stat">CPU</td><td>Intel Core 2 Quad CPU Q6600 @ 2.40GHz / AMD Phenom 9850 @ 2.5GHz</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="stat">GPU</td><td>NVIDIA 9800 GT 1GB / AMD HD 4870 1GB / Intel HD GT2</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="stat">RAM</td><td>8GB</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="stat">HDD</td><td>72GB + ~4GB for NSM cache</td></tr>
          </table>
        </article>
      </div>
      <div class="sud-note" style="margin-top:1.15rem">
        <span class="i">i</span>
        <span>NSM does not modify your Grand Theft Auto V installation files and never interacts with Rockstar Online Services other than validating your game ownership on startup.</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sud-section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="spacer">
      <p class="sud-eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span>FOR DEVELOPERS</p>
      <h2 class="sud-h2">Create a server.<br><span class="grad">Write the rules.</span></h2>
      <p class="sud-lead">Creating your own server for NSM is easy, and if you know any of the supported languages you can get started writing scripts right away. Issue a license key in AFX Portal and launch <code>NSM-Server.exe</code>.</p>
      <div class="sud-btn-row">
        <a class="btn primary" href="/keymaster">Create a server</a>
        <a class="sud-ghost" href="/docs#server-setup">Setting up a server</a>
      </div>
      <div class="sud-grid cols-3" style="margin-top:1.65rem">
        <a class="sud-card" href="/docs#scripting" style="text-decoration:none">
          <span class="sud-tag">Lua</span>
          <h3>Lua</h3>
          <p>Lightweight, fast scripting with immediate access to all GTA V &amp; AFX natives.</p>
        </a>
        <a class="sud-card" href="/docs#scripting" style="text-decoration:none">
          <span class="sud-tag">C#</span>
          <h3>C#</h3>
          <p>Strongly-typed .NET runtime for structured client and server resource development.</p>
        </a>
        <a class="sud-card" href="/docs#scripting" style="text-decoration:none">
          <span class="sud-tag">JavaScript</span>
          <h3>JavaScript</h3>
          <p>Modern V8 / Node.js runtime with TypeScript definitions and NUI integration.</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sud-section tight" id="faq">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="spacer">
      <p class="sud-sublabel">a little more clarity</p>
      <h2 class="sud-h2">Good questions.<br><span class="grad">Straight answers.</span></h2>
      <div style="margin-top:1.85rem">
        <div class="sud-faq-item" id="q1">
          <h3><a href="#q1">Will I get banned from GTA:Online for playing NSM?</a></h3>
          <p>Nope! NSM does not modify your Grand Theft Auto V installation files and never interacts with Rockstar Online Services other than validating your game ownership on startup.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sud-faq-item" id="q2">
          <h3><a href="#q2">How do I sign in inside NSM.exe?</a></h3>
          <p>Click <strong>Sign in</strong> inside <code>NSM.exe</code>. It will open the NSM website in your browser where you can sign in to your AFX account and automatically link your session back into <code>NSM.exe</code>.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sud-faq-item" id="q3">
          <h3><a href="#q3">How do I create a server and register a license key?</a></h3>
          <p>Open <a href="/keymaster">AFX Portal</a>, sign in to your account, generate a <code>cfxk_...</code> license key, and paste <code>sv_licenseKey</code> into your server's <code>server.cfg</code>.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sud-faq-item" id="q4">
          <h3><a href="#q4">Why does Steam show me playing Source SDK Base 2007?</a></h3>
          <p>Like the classic modification runtime, NSM initializes Steam integrations under App ID <code>218</code> (<strong>Source SDK Base 2007</strong>) so your Steam overlay, friends list, and rich presence work cleanly without conflicting with the base game.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sud-cta">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="spacer">
      <p class="sud-eyebrow" style="justify-content:center"><span class="dot"></span>READY WHEN YOU ARE</p>
      <h2 class="sud-h2">Make yourself <span class="grad">at home.</span></h2>
      <p class="sud-lead">Your next server starts here.</p>
      <div class="sud-btn-row">
        <a class="btn primary" href="/download">Download for Windows</a>
        <a class="sud-ghost" href="/servers">Take a look around</a>
      </div>
      <p class="sud-meta">Windows 10 &amp; 11 &nbsp;·&nbsp; 64-bit &nbsp;·&nbsp; free to play</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

